docs/research/2026-07-01-daily-labor-staffing.md:16:**Wage composition:**  Specific roles (e.g. supervisors) earn more than minimum laborers; using ~$18/hr as a baseline for general workers is reasonable (primary data from NASS).  We flag normal wages as “base pay.”  **Overtime:**  Not mandated federally (ag workers are exempt from FLSA OT (Primary)), but in practice farms often pay **1.5×** regular rate for hours beyond 40/week, especially during busy periods.  Some states (e.g. CA/NY) have earlier OT rules, but as of FY2025 overtime pay for farm workers remains largely discretionary.  **Temp/Contract Labor:**  Many farms use H-2A or local agencies for extra help.  The federal AEWR gives a floor (~$18.12 in 2024).  Agency/contract labor often pays at or above that rate (plus agency fees).  
